WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.830
- All right, it's always
nice to end the show

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:02.973
with one last bit of happiness

00:00:02.973 --> 00:00:04.133
I found on social media.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.769
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.769 --> 00:00:08.790
(upbeat music)
(crowd cheering)

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:11.790
I'm super passionate about
getting my kids to read

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:15.240
and they like it, and here
they are this morning.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.073
Yep.
(crowd awing)

00:00:16.073 --> 00:00:17.580
That's how, like you walk in their room

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.870
and they were reading to each other.

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:21.199
And I was like, look, I
didn't completely screw up.

00:00:21.199 --> 00:00:23.610
(crowd laughing)
But not all kids

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.490
have someone outside school
pushing them to pick up books.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.350
That's why a former New York teacher

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.963
is filling hundreds of barbershops,

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:32.190
coast to coast, with reading materials

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:34.680
that pique kids' minds
and creative thinking,

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:35.820
which is super important.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.500
It's a great initiative to highlight

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.270
as we prepare for giving Tuesday.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:40.920
From Barbershop Books, let's everybody

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.004
say hello to Alvin
watching on NBC New York.

00:00:44.004 --> 00:00:47.640
(crowd cheering)
Hi Alvin.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.180
Oh we have several of
those books in my house.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:51.810
My kids love Captain Underpants.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.790
So, so tell everybody what this is

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.590
and the origin story of it.

00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:59.730
- Barbershop Books' mission
is to inspire Black boys

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.970
and other vulnerable
children to read for fun,

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:06.270
and also to identify as readers.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:08.290
We create child-friendly reading spaces

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.010
in Black barbershops

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:13.200
and other barbershops across the country.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.990
And we provide early
literacy training to barbers.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:18.990
About 10 years ago, I
was getting a haircut

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:20.400
across the street from the school

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.690
where I taught first grade.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:25.320
And one of my students
came into the barbershop

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:28.080
and he got a little antsy,
he looked a little bored.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.160
And I just kept thinking,

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.124
oh I wish I had a
children's book to give him.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.570
And so, you know, understanding

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.340
the cultural significance
of the barbershop

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.440
inspired me to create Barbershop Books.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:38.483
- I love it man.

00:01:38.483 --> 00:01:40.410
So this is more than about reading,

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:41.970
it's about community, right?

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:42.803
- Yeah.

00:01:42.803 --> 00:01:45.570
For many Black boys,
they have limited access

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:48.242
to Black male reading role models.

00:01:48.242 --> 00:01:53.242
Less than 2% of teachers are Black males

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:57.120
and a majority of Black boys
are raised by a single mother.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.250
And so there's a lack
of reading role models

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.860
at school and at home, but they go

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:04.020
to the barbershop once or twice a month.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.840
And so it creates this unique opportunity

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.400
to promote reading.
- Yeah,

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.630
it's an interesting space to read.

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:11.520
And what a smart thing too, 'cause yeah

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.080
we're always taking our
kids to get their haircuts.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.551
That's awesome for them
to be able to do that,

00:02:14.551 --> 00:02:16.620
instead of just like the coloring section.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.970
You know? It's very cool.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:18.870
Thank you Alvin.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.250
This is such a cool initiative.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:21.330
I'm liking your post right now,

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:22.859
all right?
(bell dings)

00:02:22.859 --> 00:02:24.561
(crowd cheering)
All right everybody,

00:02:24.561 --> 00:02:25.394
that's not all.

00:02:25.394 --> 00:02:27.032
Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:27.032 --> 00:02:28.950
makers of Frixion, the go-to erasable pen

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.840
of "The Kelly Clarkson
Show," want to celebrate

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.810
those creating another generation
of readers just like you.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:36.330
So they're giving Barbershop
Books a thousand dollars,

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:37.576
just to help out with material.

00:02:37.576 --> 00:02:39.614
(crowd cheering)

00:02:39.614 --> 00:02:41.277
- Thanks, I appreciate it.

00:02:41.277 --> 00:02:42.123
- Thank you Alvin.

00:02:42.123 --> 00:02:44.647
And thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:02:44.647 --> 00:02:47.982
Kevin Bacon, Ego Nwodim, Lawrence Zarian,

00:02:47.982 --> 00:02:48.815
and Kevin Quinn.

00:02:48.815 --> 00:02:49.648
Y'all have a great day.
(crowd cheering)

00:02:49.648 --> 00:02:51.737
And if it's not, try and change it.

